  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "CLEAT and ReqClarifyBench both introduce frameworks for evaluating interactive requirement clarification in software development. CLEAT focuses on aligning LLMs with user intent through clarification, while ReqClarifyBench tests how LLMs can transform vague user intent into clear requirements across different development scenarios.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "CLEAT introduces a clarification-value controller and task policy co-training framework to improve interaction with LLMs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "ReqClarifyBench evaluates LLMs on tasks spanning game, miniapp, and web development, with a focus on software development rather than function-level tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "CLEAT achieves higher mean scores in all ten evaluation settings across four benchmarks with Qwen3-4B, while ReqClarifyBench shows varying performance based on user personas.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
